ehr-testing-sim -- resources/demographics/ provenance notice
==============================================================

docs/third-party-sources.md names Synthea (Apache-2.0, MITRE) as the
mined source for this project's US demographics tables
(demographics-tables, docs/sim-theory.edn's Persona catalytic), on the
strength of Synthea's own vendored name/geography data. Milestone M4's
authoring session checked for a `../` sibling Synthea checkout to
extract that data from, per this session's own instructions, and found
none present (only ehr-testing-tools' `config/synthea/synthea.properties`
-- a runner config file, not vendored demographic data). AGENTS.md's
standing rule ("do not invent facts about upstream sources") applies
here as much as anywhere else in this repo: absent an actual checkout
to extract from, the tables in this directory
(given-names.edn, surnames.edn, places.edn) are HAND-CURATED originals
authored by this session, not copied, adapted, or algorithmically
derived from any Synthea file.

What IS carried from Synthea, honestly: the SCHEMA SHAPE these tables
use (given names bucketed by sex and birth decade, a flat weighted
surname pool, sampled geography rows) mirrors the general design of
Synthea's own demographic sampling approach, as already described in
docs/operational-models.md's payers-model section and
docs/third-party-sources.md's Synthea entry -- mining for *design*, not
data, the same distinction ADR-0002 already draws for Google Simulated
Hospital. A future session WITH a Synthea checkout available can
replace the content of these three files wholesale with a real
extraction, keeping ehr-testing-sim.persona's readers unchanged, since
the schema is already shaped to match.

This file exists so a reader of this directory never has to guess
whether "vendored from Synthea" means "copied from Synthea" here -- it
doesn't, and this notice is the record of that distinction, dated to
the session that made the call.

Recorded: 2026-07-26. All content is synthetic; no PHI, no real-person
data, by construction (this repo's standing constraint,
docs/problem-statement.md / AGENTS.md).
